_padj":0.683527,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000077684","entrez_id":["79960"],"uniprot":["Q6IE81"],"ncbi_summary":"Enables transcription coactivator activity. Involved in histone acetylation and negative regulation of canonical Wnt signaling pathway. Acts upstream of or within negative regulation of G1/S transition of mitotic cell cycle. Located in several cellular components, including ciliary basal body; cytosol; and nuclear speck. Part of histone acetyltransferase complex. [provided by Alliance of Genome Resources, Apr 2022]","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q6IE81","text":"Scaffold subunit of some HBO1 complexes, which have a histone H4 acetyltransferase activity (PubMed:16387653, PubMed:19187766, PubMed:20129055, PubMed:24065767). Plays a key role in HBO1 complex by directing KAT7/HBO1 specificity towards histone H4 acetylation (H4K5ac, H4K8ac and H4K12ac), regulating DNA replication initiation, regulating DNA replication initiation (PubMed:20129055, PubMed:24065767). May also promote acetylation of nucleosomal histone H4 by KAT5 (PubMed:15502158). Promotes apoptosis (PubMed:16046545). May act as a renal tumor suppressor (PubMed:16046545). Negatively regulates canonical Wnt signaling; at least in part, cooperates with NPHP4 in this function (PubMed:22654112)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}